{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CghrjEhdnqHYiCF2xY8LC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VqDQrZStch1v2HWGDswi8F","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261104-050256__x4339a3/work/MashTV-SmashTV-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-050256; sed -n '1220,1254p;1047,1078p' handoff/API-INDEX.md","description":"Read arcade module and audio sections of API-INDEX"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11973,"cache_read_input_tokens":195779,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11973},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"320246ab-3447-463f-809e-86ed7a6b39d9","uuid":"f3fc431b-63f8-43f2-8a7f-61fc7fb756e1","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:05:55.967Z","request_id":"req_011CghrjEMYXjmsKM8fAK7P4","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01VqDQrZStch1v2HWGDswi8F":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261104-050256__x4339a3/work/MashTV-SmashTV-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-050256; sed -n '1220,1254p;1047,1078p' handoff/API-INDEX.md","description":"Read arcade module and audio sections of API-INDEX"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VqDQrZStch1v2HWGDswi8F","type":"tool_result","content":"## 20. Audio\n\n- `E.note(n)`: note name -> frequency: E.note('A4') = 440, E.note('C#5'), E.note('Bb2'). Numbers pass through\n- `E.songs: title, adventure, dungeon, boss, victory`: ready-made chiptune loops (original compositions). game.audio.music('adventure')\n- `game.audio.applyVolume()`: apply volume, musicVolume, sfxVolume and mute after setting them directly (setVolume and mute call it)\n- `game.audio.at(step, fn)` †: call fn(step) on the update step the music reaches step (counted from its start, on as it loops); the song's change cancels it. Returns { cancel() }\n- `game.audio.calibrate()` †: the audio offset's calibration: a click on each beat (100 bpm, the first of a bar higher) as the music; tap(time) on each one heard (an event's timeStamp, or nothing: this update step). After 8 taps, result is the offset to set (ms: settings.audioOffset) and done is true; taps go on refining it. stop() puts the music back\n- `game.audio.define(name, voice)`: add or replace a named sound: audio.define('zap', { wave: 'saw', freq: 1200, to: 200, dur: .2 })\n- `game.audio.duck(on = true)`: quiet the music (to 35%) while on: under a game's own pause, map or dialog screen. The engine also ducks it while game.paused\n- `game.audio.layer(track, vol = 1, fade = .5)` †: a track's volume as the song plays, 0..1, faded over fade seconds: layers of one song (the chase's drums in when the guards see you, out when they lose you). track: its index in song.tracks, or its name\n- `game.audio.music(song, o = {})`: Loop a song (or play once with { loop: false }). song = { bpm: 120, steps: 4, tracks: [ { wave: 'square', vol: .2, notes: 'C5 - E5 - G5 - . . | ...' }, one token per step { wave: 'triangle', notes: 'C3 . C3 . G2 . G2 .' }, { wave: 'drums', notes: 'k . h . s . h . k k h . s . h .' } ] } tokens: C4 F#3 Bb2 = note, '-' holds the previous note, '.' = rest, '|' is ignored (bar lines). steps = steps per beat (4 = sixteenth notes). Each track loops on its own length within the song's (len: steps, else its longest track's); a track may have a name, and on: false starts it silent (a layer that audio.layer brings in). THE MUSIC CLOCK: a song starts at the game's time and where it is is game time (audio.pos, headless too: the same steps hear the same beats); the sound follows that clock. o: { loop, sync: true (it pauses with the game, on game.time; else it plays on through a pause, on game.real), fade: seconds (a crossfade from the song playing), restart: true (again from its start, though it is the one playing) }. E.songs has ready-made loops: title, adventure, dungeon, boss, victory.\n- `game.audio.mute(on = !this.muted)`: toggle (or set) mute; returns the new state\n- `game.audio.onBeat(fn)` †: call fn(beat, pos) on the update step of each beat of whatever music plays (a dancer's step, a light's pulse). Returns { cancel() }\n- `game.audio.pos` †: where the music is, on the game's clock (headless too): { t: seconds since it started, step (from 0, counting on as it loops), beat, bar (four beats), at (the step in its loop), loop (times round), bpm, layers (each track's volume), playing }\n- `game.audio.ready`: true once the browser lets the game make sound\n- `game.audio.setVolume(v)`: set the master volume, 0..1\n- `game.audio.sfx(what, o = {})`: Play a sound effect: a preset name ('jump', 'coin', 'hit', 'explode', ...), a voice object, or a list of voices. opts: { vol: 0..1, pitch: multiplier, vary: random pitch spread (default 0.03), step: a step of the music playing (it sounds on that step of the music clock, scheduled with the music: a rhythm game's calls and claps) }\n- `game.audio.sting(song, o = {})` †: play a short song once over the music (a goal's jingle): o.at 'now', 'beat' or 'bar' (on the music's next beat or bar), o.duck (the music's volume under it, .4)\n- `game.audio.stopMusic(fade)`: stop the music (it fades out over fade seconds, .06 by default)\n- `game.audio.tempo(bpm)` †: change the music's tempo as it plays (hurry up!): where it is stays, the steps after come at the new bpm\n- `game.audio.anchors = 0` †: how many times the sound was moved to meet the clock\n- `game.audio.ctx = null`: the Web Audio context, made at the first sound (null before, or where there is none)\n- `game.audio.drift = 0` †: what is heard against the game's clock at the last frame (seconds: the sound follows the clock, so it stays near 0)\n- `game.audio.ducked = false`: true while duck(true) holds the music down\n- `game.audio.failed = null`: why there is no sound (a message), or null\n- `game.audio.musicVolume = .5`, `game.audio.sfxVolume = 1`: 0..1 for effects and music\n- `game.audio.muted = false`: true while mute() is on\n- `game.audio.offset = 0` †: seconds the music sounds early, for speakers and headphones that lag (settings.audioOffset)\n- `game.audio.presets`: the named sound effects, sfx(name) plays one and define(name, voice) adds one\n- `game.audio.song = null`: the music playing (null for none)\n- `game.audio.volume = .7`: master volume 0..1\n\n## Module arcade: the coin-op's frame: scores, high-score tables and initials, lives, credits, turns, cards, the attract mode (engine/modules/arcade.js)\n\n- `new E.Arcade(game, o = {}) → arcade`: new E.Arcade(game, { id, lives: 3, extra: [] (the scores that give a life) or every (a life each that many points), credits: null (free play) or the coins a game takes, idle: 20, demo: 30, scores: 6 (the attract mode's seconds), hud: true, colors: [label, number, highlight] })\n- `arcade.add(points, at)`: add points to the player up (at: a world point { x, y, z } where they float up); an extra life at each threshold\n- `arcade.attract(dt)`: the attract mode, each step on the title: 'title', 'demo' (o.idle seconds without input; it lasts o.demo seconds or until endDemo()), 'scores' (o.scores seconds), then 'title' again; any input goes back to 'title'\n- `arcade.card(text, seconds = 2)`: a card in the middle of the screen for seconds ('STAGE 2', 'PLAYER 2, READY!')\n- `arcade.carding`: is a card up? (hold play while it is)\n- `arcade.clear()`: take every card and word down\n- `arcade.coin()`: add a coin (credits on); returns the credits\n- `arcade.continue(seconds = 10, done)`: a continue: CONTINUE? counts down seconds; start, confirm or a tap continues (with the credits it takes): every player's lives back, the scores kept, done(true); at zero, done(false)\n- `arcade.continuing`: is the continue counting down?\n- `arcade.die()`: a life lost: 'again' (lives left), 'next' (the other player's turn) or 'over' (none left for anyone)\n- `arcade.draw(r, box)`: the frame over the game, after its drawing: the HUD (o.hud: 1UP, HI, 2UP in a row) along the top of box [x, y, w, h] (the playfield; the screen when none), the lives along its foot, the cards, DEMO, the continue and the entry\n- `arcade.drawTable(r, mode = '', y = 40, title = 'HIGH SCORES')`: a table as a screen (the attract mode's, or after a game), its title at y: rank, name, score\n- `arcade.endDemo()`: the demo is over (a demo in a scene of its own: call it on the way back): the attract mode shows the scores\n- `arcade.enter(score, mode = '', done)`: open the initials entry for score; done(name) once it is taken and saved\n- `arcade.qualifies(score, mode = '')`: would score make the top ten (never in a demo)?\n- `arcade.say(text, seconds = 1.2)`: a short word under the cards for seconds ('READY!', 'EXTRA LIFE!')\n- `arcade.start(players = 1, o = {})`: begin a game for 1 or 2 players (taking turns), o: { demo: true } for the attract mode's; spends the credits a game takes unless it is free play or a demo. Returns false without them\n- `arcade.table(mode = '')`: the top ten of a mode: [{ name, score }]\n- `arcade.update(dt)`: a step: the cards count down, the entry and the continue read the keys\n- `arcade.wake()`: the attract mode back to the title, its idle clock at zero (as any input does)\n- `arcade.credits`: coins in (null: free play)\n- `arcade.demo = false`: a demo is playing (no table)\n- `arcade.entry = null`: the initials being entered ({ score, mode, name, i }), or null\n- `arcade.game`: the game it serves\n- `arcade.hi = 0`: the high score shown\n- `arcade.id`: the game's name (its tables')\n- `arcade.mode = 'title'`: 'title' | 'play' | 'over'\n- `arcade.o`: the options\n- `arcade.p = null`: the player up\n- `arcade.phase = 'title'`: the attract mode's, 'title' | 'demo' | 'scores'\n- `arcade.players = []`: [{ n, score, lives, save (the game's own: a stage kept while the other plays), next (the score of the next extra life) }]\n- `arcade.wheel = null`: where the letter wheel was last drawn (taps answer to it): { x, y, cw, up, down, ok } in screen pixels: three columns cw wide from x, the up and down bands [y0, y1], the OK button [x, y, w, h]","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"320246ab-3447-463f-809e-86ed7a6b39d9","uuid":"f195af87-7c1a-4994-a6ac-d89ab75a4823","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:05:55.981Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"## 20. Audio\n\n- `E.note(n)`: note name -> frequency: E.note('A4') = 440, E.note('C#5'), E.note('Bb2'). Numbers pass through\n- `E.songs: title, adventure, dungeon, boss, victory`: ready-made chiptune loops (original compositions). game.audio.music('adventure')\n- `game.audio.applyVolume()`: apply volume, musicVolume, sfxVolume and mute after setting them directly (setVolume and mute call it)\n- `game.audio.at(step, fn)` †: call fn(step) on the update step the music reaches step (counted from its start, on as it loops); the song's change cancels it. Returns { cancel() }\n- `game.audio.calibrate()` †: the audio offset's calibration: a click on each beat (100 bpm, the first of a bar higher) as the music; tap(time) on each one heard (an event's timeStamp, or nothing: this update step). After 8 taps, result is the offset to set (ms: settings.audioOffset) and done is true; taps go on refining it. stop() puts the music back\n- `game.audio.define(name, voice)`: add or replace a named sound: audio.define('zap', { wave: 'saw', freq: 1200, to: 200, dur: .2 })\n- `game.audio.duck(on = true)`: quiet the music (to 35%) while on: under a game's own pause, map or dialog screen. The engine also ducks it while game.paused\n- `game.audio.layer(track, vol = 1, fade = .5)` †: a track's volume as the song plays, 0..1, faded over fade seconds: layers of one song (the chase's drums in when the guards see you, out when they lose you). track: its index in song.tracks, or its name\n- `game.audio.music(song, o = {})`: Loop a song (or play once with { loop: false }). song = { bpm: 120, steps: 4, tracks: [ { wave: 'square', vol: .2, notes: 'C5 - E5 - G5 - . . | ...' }, one token per step { wave: 'triangle', notes: 'C3 . C3 . G2 . G2 .' }, { wave: 'drums', notes: 'k . h . s . h . k k h . s . h .' } ] } tokens: C4 F#3 Bb2 = note, '-' holds the previous note, '.' = rest, '|' is ignored (bar lines). steps = steps per beat (4 = sixteenth notes). Each track loops on its own length within the song's (len: steps, else its longest track's); a track may have a name, and on: false starts it silent (a layer that audio.layer brings in). THE MUSIC CLOCK: a song starts at the game's time and where it is is game time (audio.pos, headless too: the same steps hear the same beats); the sound follows that clock. o: { loop, sync: true (it pauses with the game, on game.time; else it plays on through a pause, on game.real), fade: seconds (a crossfade from the song playing), restart: true (again from its start, though it is the one playing) }. E.songs has ready-made loops: title, adventure, dungeon, boss, victory.\n- `game.audio.mute(on = !this.muted)`: toggle (or set) mute; returns the new state\n- `game.audio.onBeat(fn)` †: call fn(beat, pos) on the update step of each beat of whatever music plays (a dancer's step, a light's pulse). Returns { cancel() }\n- `game.audio.pos` †: where the music is, on the game's clock (headless too): { t: seconds since it started, step (from 0, counting on as it loops), beat, bar (four beats), at (the step in its loop), loop (times round), bpm, layers (each track's volume), playing }\n- `game.audio.ready`: true once the browser lets the game make sound\n- `game.audio.setVolume(v)`: set the master volume, 0..1\n- `game.audio.sfx(what, o = {})`: Play a sound effect: a preset name ('jump', 'coin', 'hit', 'explode', ...), a voice object, or a list of voices. opts: { vol: 0..1, pitch: multiplier, vary: random pitch spread (default 0.03), step: a step of the music playing (it sounds on that step of the music clock, scheduled with the music: a rhythm game's calls and claps) }\n- `game.audio.sting(song, o = {})` †: play a short song once over the music (a goal's jingle): o.at 'now', 'beat' or 'bar' (on the music's next beat or bar), o.duck (the music's volume under it, .4)\n- `game.audio.stopMusic(fade)`: stop the music (it fades out over fade seconds, .06 by default)\n- `game.audio.tempo(bpm)` †: change the music's tempo as it plays (hurry up!): where it is stays, the steps after come at the new bpm\n- `game.audio.anchors = 0` †: how many times the sound was moved to meet the clock\n- `game.audio.ctx = null`: the Web Audio context, made at the first sound (null before, or where there is none)\n- `game.audio.drift = 0` †: what is heard against the game's clock at the last frame (seconds: the sound follows the clock, so it stays near 0)\n- `game.audio.ducked = false`: true while duck(true) holds the music down\n- `game.audio.failed = null`: why there is no sound (a message), or null\n- `game.audio.musicVolume = .5`, `game.audio.sfxVolume = 1`: 0..1 for effects and music\n- `game.audio.muted = false`: true while mute() is on\n- `game.audio.offset = 0` †: seconds the music sounds early, for speakers and headphones that lag (settings.audioOffset)\n- `game.audio.presets`: the named sound effects, sfx(name) plays one and define(name, voice) adds one\n- `game.audio.song = null`: the music playing (null for none)\n- `game.audio.volume = .7`: master volume 0..1\n\n## Module arcade: the coin-op's frame: scores, high-score tables and initials, lives, credits, turns, cards, the attract mode (engine/modules/arcade.js)\n\n- `new E.Arcade(game, o = {}) → arcade`: new E.Arcade(game, { id, lives: 3, extra: [] (the scores that give a life) or every (a life each that many points), credits: null (free play) or the coins a game takes, idle: 20, demo: 30, scores: 6 (the attract mode's seconds), hud: true, colors: [label, number, highlight] })\n- `arcade.add(points, at)`: add points to the player up (at: a world point { x, y, z } where they float up); an extra life at each threshold\n- `arcade.attract(dt)`: the attract mode, each step on the title: 'title', 'demo' (o.idle seconds without input; it lasts o.demo seconds or until endDemo()), 'scores' (o.scores seconds), then 'title' again; any input goes back to 'title'\n- `arcade.card(text, seconds = 2)`: a card in the middle of the screen for seconds ('STAGE 2', 'PLAYER 2, READY!')\n- `arcade.carding`: is a card up? (hold play while it is)\n- `arcade.clear()`: take every card and word down\n- `arcade.coin()`: add a coin (credits on); returns the credits\n- `arcade.continue(seconds = 10, done)`: a continue: CONTINUE? counts down seconds; start, confirm or a tap continues (with the credits it takes): every player's lives back, the scores kept, done(true); at zero, done(false)\n- `arcade.continuing`: is the continue counting down?\n- `arcade.die()`: a life lost: 'again' (lives left), 'next' (the other player's turn) or 'over' (none left for anyone)\n- `arcade.draw(r, box)`: the frame over the game, after its drawing: the HUD (o.hud: 1UP, HI, 2UP in a row) along the top of box [x, y, w, h] (the playfield; the screen when none), the lives along its foot, the cards, DEMO, the continue and the entry\n- `arcade.drawTable(r, mode = '', y = 40, title = 'HIGH SCORES')`: a table as a screen (the attract mode's, or after a game), its title at y: rank, name, score\n- `arcade.endDemo()`: the demo is over (a demo in a scene of its own: call it on the way back): the attract mode shows the scores\n- `arcade.enter(score, mode = '', done)`: open the initials entry for score; done(name) once it is taken and saved\n- `arcade.qualifies(score, mode = '')`: would score make the top ten (never in a demo)?\n- `arcade.say(text, seconds = 1.2)`: a short word under the cards for seconds ('READY!', 'EXTRA LIFE!')\n- `arcade.start(players = 1, o = {})`: begin a game for 1 or 2 players (taking turns), o: { demo: true } for the attract mode's; spends the credits a game takes unless it is free play or a demo. Returns false without them\n- `arcade.table(mode = '')`: the top ten of a mode: [{ name, score }]\n- `arcade.update(dt)`: a step: the cards count down, the entry and the continue read the keys\n- `arcade.wake()`: the attract mode back to the title, its idle clock at zero (as any input does)\n- `arcade.credits`: coins in (null: free play)\n- `arcade.demo = false`: a demo is playing (no table)\n- `arcade.entry = null`: the initials being entered ({ score, mode, name, i }), or null\n- `arcade.game`: the game it serves\n- `arcade.hi = 0`: the high score shown\n- `arcade.id`: the game's name (its tables')\n- `arcade.mode = 'title'`: 'title' | 'play' | 'over'\n- `arcade.o`: the options\n- `arcade.p = null`: the player up\n- `arcade.phase = 'title'`: the attract mode's, 'title' | 'demo' | 'scores'\n- `arcade.players = []`: [{ n, score, lives, save (the game's own: a stage kept while the other plays), next (the score of the next extra life) }]\n- `arcade.wheel = null`: where the letter wheel was last drawn (taps answer to it): { x, y, cw, up, down, ok } in screen pixels: three columns cw wide from x, the up and down bands [y0, y1], the OK button [x, y, w, h]","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"to