{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\n<system-reminder>\n<tools-used-before-summary>Bash, Edit, Read, ToolSearch, Write</tools-used-before-summary>\n</system-reminder>\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   - **The /goal:** \"Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says (TASK.md describes the game). Done when: the bundled single .html file exists in this folder's root, every feature in TASK.md is implemented with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs, exit-interview.json in this folder's root parses as JSON and answers every field, and your final reply contains the Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections.\"\n   - **STAGE.md:** \"Read TASK.md (what to build) and PLAN.md (how to build it…) … Build the game TASK.md describes, following the plan and using the title it gives; where they disagree, TASK.md wins. Deliver everything TASK.md asks for, including its file name, and the sections it asks for in your final reply.\"\n   - **TASK.md requirements:**\n     - an original game inspired by Smash TV, packaged as a single HTML file named `GameTitle-SOURCE-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-050256.html`, with a dev subfolder of the same name;\n     - built on the my-3d2dge handoff, using its native art and animation style plus new assets;\n     - all audio in code, with Animalese/Simlish-style gibberish voices;\n     - AI Hub multiplayer and standalone co-op;\n     - a dev mode in the pause menu with live sliders and a reset to defaults (\"Balance is key\");\n     - an attract mode after 10 s idle that any input exits;\n     - a 10-foot, controller-first UI: PlayStation glyphs with an Xbox option, native keyboard and mouse, prompts that follow the last input, no dense screens;\n     - touch-only devices: show \"Controller or keyboard required\" plus a settings button, and let the attract mode run;\n     - no TODOs or stubs;\n     - an in-game About screen and a chat reply with Source Information, Testing, Engine and Prompt Feedback;\n     - exit-interview.json in the exact shape given.\n   - **Constraints from TASK.md, verbatim:**\n     - \"Do not read files outside what you need - other agents share this directory. They share this machine's ports and processes too. Prefer file:// and the engine's headless tools. If you need a server (the AI Hub harness does), bind 127.0.0.1 on a port the OS picks (`python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1` prints it) and confirm the page is your game before trusting a result. Stop only processes you started, by their PID: never pkill, killall, fuser -k, or kill whatever holds a port.\"\n     - \"Don't use subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit.\"\n     - \"Keep them [tests] behind one command that prints only failures and a one-line count, and rerun it only after changing the code it covers. Use screenshots only for what a script can't check.\"\n   - **Email:** the user's email (michael@dealermedia.com) must only be used for identification, never sent to services.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - **Engine basics:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2 full edition (`E = My3D2dge`), headless Node `vm` testing, `game.advance` fixed 1/120 s steps, `input.tap/press/feed`, `game.debug`.\n   - **Engine systems used:** TileMap, Humanoid and Blob rigs, `r.actor/queue/sprite/shape/decal`, canvas lighting, particles, E.Bullets, E.Arcade, E.Shell pause and settings, `game.settings.define`, `allowJoin/addPlayer`, E.SHAPES assets plus a cut store set (`assets/mash-props.js`).\n   - **AI Hub:**\n     - Session Protocol v1, shared-world mode, client session.js 1.4.0 inlined verbatim as the first `<head>` script.\n     - Host-authoritative world with 15/s snapshots, client prediction, 120 ms interpolation, claims and hurt reports, room messages, `finish` with standings and awards, and server mode.\n     - Message limits: at most 20 a second and 16 KB each.\n   - **Game architecture:**\n     - Every module is a fragment of one IIFE.\n     - Content is data: `MT.ROOMS`, `MT.EPISODES`, `MT.ENEMIES`, `MT.WEAPONS`, `MT.TEXT`.\n     - Tuning registry `MT.TDEF`/`MT.T`; event bus plus a reaction table.\n     - A custom coroutine runner (`Co`), a World with phases, input presets `MASH_MENU`/`MASH_PLAY` with a preset-sync hook.\n   - **Babble:** formant synthesis on the engine's audio context, routed through the effects bus.\n   - **Rendering pitfall:** sprites scale by camera zoom only, so world sprites need `scale: 1/zoom`.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections (all in the dev folder unless noted):\n   - **`engine/my-3d2dge.js`:** the handoff engine with patches P1–P4, applied by `tools/patch-engine.mjs`:\n     - P1: `E.HOOKS = HOOKS;`\n     - P2: the glyphs setting defaults to PlayStation with Xbox as the only option, and its `apply` sets every player; `addPlayer` copies `q.glyphs = P[0].glyphs`.\n     - P3: `Arcade.enter(score, mode, done, input)`; `continue()` accepts any player's input.\n     - P4: `get bus() { return this.ctx ? this._sfxBus : null; }`.\n   - **`engine/PATCHES.md`:** documents P1–P4.\n   - **`tools/build.mjs`:**\n     - `export const OUT = 'MashTV-SmashTV-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-050256'`.\n     - Concatenates `src/*.js` into `build/game.js`, inlines about.json, runs `node --check`.\n     - Writes the deliverable (hub metas, page.css, session.js first, splash, canvas, engine, props, game), `build/dev.html`, and `../exit-interview.json` from `about.exitInterview`.\n   - **`tools/test.mjs`:** runner (`--only`, `--no-browser`); prints failures plus \"MASH TV tests: N passed, M failed\".\n   - **`tools/harness.mjs`:** `boot(o)` creates a vm context (console, timers, localStorage stub, optional hub and globals), loads the engine, props (with a temporary `window`) and game.\n   - **`tools/fakehub.mjs`:** `createHub({players, server, latency, jitter, loss})` with tick, card, start, leave, timeUp and end.\n   - **Other tools:** `tools/balance.mjs` (args: rooms, players, diff, tunes JSON; `SEED` env), `shot.mjs`, `probe.mjs`, `spawnshot.mjs`, `audiocheck.mjs`, `e2e.mjs`, `e2e-debug.mjs`.\n   - **Source modules:**\n     - `src/00-core.js`: geometry (AR, DOORS, cellW), the seeded RNG streams, TDEF tunings, cheats, the bus, helpers.\n     - `src/01-input.js`: presets, the preset hook, `intentFrom`, the idle detector (`MT.wheelTake`; a mouse move over 8 px sets lastDevice to 'mouse'), `MT.touchOnly`.\n     - `src/02-glyphs.js`: pixel glyph icons, `GLYPH.draw/drawCode/prompt/describe`.\n     - `src/03-audio-music.js`: 8 songs and 12 stings.\n     - `src/04-audio-sfx.js`: about 70 sounds.\n     - `src/05-babble.js`: voices and the crowd.\n     - `src/06-art-studio.js`: sets, shapes `mt:*`, the audience, jumbotron, doors, lights (including the Prime Time strobe), fireworks.\n     - `src/07-art-chars.js`: looks and rigs.\n     - `src/08-sprites.js`: sprites plus `unzoom(r)`.\n     - `src/10-arena.js`: Arena; door cells hidden in `queueWalls`; `fitCamera` (zoom about 0.6); hazards.\n     - `src/11-contestant.js`, `src/12-weapons.js`, `src/13-enemies.js`, `src/14-pickups.js` (pedestals), `src/15-ratings.js`.\n     - `src/16-waves.js`: Co runner (a bare yield means the next step), the `waveGap` early guard, the `keyOn` spawn option, `MT.scaleAdds`, the survive script (two doors per 1.2 s).\n     - `src/17-bosses.js`: the Boss framework (setPhase is guarded once dying; parts are unhittable during intro), Mashy (body 130, arms 36, `onArmDown` only in p1, `skipIntro`), Wheel, Finale.\n     - `src/18-world.js`: the World (final-key drop, confetti and scorch decals, session-safe hit effects, hurry with 4 clapbots).\n     - `src/19-react.js`, `src/20-content-episodes.js` (rooms, including the extra waves in 1-2 and 1-6, survive time 40), `src/21-content-script.js`.\n     - `src/30-ui-kit.js`: hover by pointer movement, wheel scrolling.\n     - `src/31-hud.js`, `src/32-screens.js` (frontStep resets idle on scene entry; `frontCam`; recap resets `finished`; Game Over draws lying rigs with `pose:'down'`).\n     - `src/33-dev.js`, `src/34-cutscenes.js`, `src/40-bot.js` (the human option, noFire, separation), `src/41-attract.js`, `src/50-net.js`, `src/60-play.js` (camera updated every step; skippable boss intros; the intense layer; crowd murmur).\n     - `src/90-main.js`: game creation, SETTINGS, deep links, `game.debug`, the boot scene; contains the latest fix:\n     ```js\n     function leavePause() { if (game.shell && game.shell.screen) game.shell.hide(); game.resume(); if (HAS_DOM && document.activeElement && document.activeElement.blur) document.activeElement.blur(); for (const p of game.players) p.consumeAll(); }\n     function pauseOverlay(who, ov) { const sc = game.scene; const was = sc.pausable; sc.pausable = false; MT.overlay.open = true; MT.overlay.who = who; ov.t = 0; const step = ov.step;\n       ov.update = function (dt) { this.t += dt; const toMenu = this.t > .15 && game.players.some(q => q.map.pause && q.pressed('pause')), toPlay = this.t > .15 && !toMenu && game.players.some(q => q.map.cancel && q.pressed('cancel')); if (toMenu || toPlay) { MT.sfx('back'); this.toMenu = toMenu; return false; } if (step) step.call(this, dt); return true; };\n       ov.done = () => { MT.overlay.open = false; MT.overlay.who = null; sc.pausable = was; for (const q of game.players) q.consumeAll(); if (ov.toMenu) game.pause('player'); }; PLAY.show(ov); }\n     ```\n     - The pause items are Dev mode, Episode map and How to play; each calls `leavePause()` first.\n   - **`src/about.json`:** About content and the exitInterview. It holds the final feedback (28 issues, 4 critical) and the usage estimate (\"about 160K output tokens… Session time about 2 h 20 min (05:03 to 07:22 MST…)\"). The testing text describes 24 suites.\n   - **Test suites (one file per area):**\n     - core, input, audio\n     - contestant, weapons, economy, ratings\n     - enemies, rooms, room-sweep\n     - bosses, playthrough\n     - ui, dev, attract, touch, proof\n     - net\n     - browser, hub\n     - balance, audio-browser\n     - features (the TASK.md audit)\n     - e2e (real-input walkthrough)\n   - **Other files:** `README.md`, `package.json` (playwright 1.63.0), and the root deliverables `../MashTV-SmashTV-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-050256.html` (about 1.72 MB) and `../exit-interview.json`.\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - **Font glyphs:** unsupported characters (·, —, −, ✓, × in the tiny font) were replaced with ASCII.\n   - **Ratings gauge:** cramped; redesigned.\n   - **Coroutine runner:** a bare yield waited two steps, running boss loops and the survive timer at half speed. Fixed so `w.step` returns true.\n   - **Prize Recap:** hung after Episode 2 because the reused scene kept `finished`. It is now reset in `enter`.\n   - **Attract mode:** stuck on reel 1 because the wipe re-armed every step. Added an `ATT.leaving` guard.\n   - **Keys:** the 'final' key rule (Pyro Pit) and the carrier key (Mascot Mayhem, via `keyOn`) were never wired. Both implemented.\n   - **Boss intros:** parts were hittable during intros. Now excluded.\n   - **Lance's reveal:** waited for the current pattern to finish. It now starts in `update` the moment the podium falls.\n   - **Net:**\n     - clients overwrote their own contestant from snapshots when a bot drove it; now skipped by netId;\n     - remote fire cooldown never counted down; now decremented;\n     - Mashy's `toNet` ran before the first sync; now robust.\n   - **Idle clock:** not reset on entering a screen, so Top Earners jumped to attract. Reset in `frontStep`.\n   - **Mouse hover:** required lastDevice to be mouse. Now driven by pointer movement.\n   - **Control names:** set only with a DOM; now set headless too.\n   - **Sprites:** drew at about 60% size because zoom was about 0.6. Fixed with `scale: unzoom(r)`.\n   - **Camera:** not updated under overlays; recap and other scenes misaligned. Camera now updated at the top of play update, plus `frontCam`.\n   - **Kill pop-ups:** flooded the screen. Now quiet below $1,000.\n   - **Materials:** invalid patterns (linen, velvet); fixed.\n   - **Mashy unkillable:** `onArmDown` called `setPhase('p2')` after death. Fixed by guarding `setPhase` when dying and only allowing the arm transition in p1.\n   - **Balance:** rooms cleared too fast and Prime Time came every room. Retuned (waveSize 1.7, spawnGap 2.2, waveGap 6, ratingsGain 0.6, decay 3), added waves, unscaled boss adds (`MT.scaleAdds`), eased Mashy and the survive room.\n   - **Dev mode keyboard (real browser):** after clicking the pause item, `game.resume()` didn't close the Shell pause screen, which held input back. Fixed with `leavePause()`.\n   - **Esc on How to play:** left the overlay open under the pause menu. Fixed with `pauseOverlay`.\n   - **Test-side issues:** fade timing, hash-only `goto` not reloading (fixed by adding `?n=`), a bot's showstopper breaking the Wheel during its test (`noFire` disables bombs), the pitch detector's octave errors (replaced with oscillator-frequency recording).\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - **Final full suite:** \"MASH TV tests: 508 passed, 0 failed (4m 11s)\".\n   - **AI Hub harness:** 4 of 4 pass.\n   - **Engine look checker:** no errors, no look notes.\n   - **Real-input e2e:** pause menu, dev sliders (95 → 105, then R reset), Esc closing, How to play and Episode map, attract at 10 s with key exit, touch-only notice with SETTINGS opening settings.\n   - **Balance:** Episode 1 rooms take about 50–57 s with 0–2 deaths for the human-like bot on seeds 9 and 21; Mashy beaten in about 125 s.\n   - **Audio measured:** songs RMS above 0.03 with peaks under 0.3; every sound produces signal; voice pitches Network 72, Announcer 99, Mashy 128, Lance 157, Penny 356 Hz.\n   - **exit-interview.json:** parses with every field filled and matches `MT.ABOUT`.\n   - **Processes:** other agents' `python3 http.server` processes (started 11+ hours ago) are not mine and were left alone.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - The /goal command (quoted in full in section 1).\n   - Repeated Stop hook feedback messages (system-generated hook output, not human). They cite gaps: the TASK.md cross-check happened afterwards, 'Balance is key' is only a self-defined bot target, audio was never judged by listening, and feature completeness rests on my own audit.\n   - The latest hook message adds: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools… Your entire response must be plain text: an <analysis> block followed by a <summary> block.\"\n   - No other genuine human messages.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - None actionable in-session.\n   - The hook's remaining demands can't be met by an agent: a human playtest, listening to the audio, and independent verification (TASK.md forbids subagent audits).\n   - All deliverables are complete.\n\n8. Current Work:\n   - All implementation is finished.\n   - The last code change was the pause-overlay rework in `src/90-main.js` (`leavePause`, `pauseOverlay`), with the e2e test updated to expect \"Esc from How to play goes back to the pause menu it came from\" and \"Backspace (cancel) closes it, straight back to play\".\n   - The final full run passed: 508 checks, 0 failed.\n   - The last replies restated completion and included all four required sections.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   - No further work is required.\n   - If continuing, only re-deliver the final reply containing the four sections: Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback, Prompt Feedback.\n   - Those sections should keep the same content: 24 suites, 508 checks, 28 issues with 4 critical, the engine patches P1–P4, and usage marked unknown plus the estimate.\n   - The remaining hook objections need a human playtest and listening, which can't be done in this session.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /home/micha/.claude/projects/-home-micha-dev-cc-matrix-runs-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-build--20261104-050256--x4339a3-work/320246ab-3447-463f-809e-86ed7a6b39d9.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened.\n\nThe messages after this summary are the most recent messages from before compaction, kept verbatim. The summary was written without seeing them, so something it says has not happened yet may already have happened in them."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"320246ab-3447-463f-809e-86ed7a6b39d9","uuid":"106ae8fa-a70d-4806-97ca-a2bd60ee385b","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:24:09.158Z","isSynthetic":true}
